WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.160
Katachi turns a photo you love into pieces you can cut.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:12.880
It’s a prototype, built this week on Meta’s models, and this film was made with Muse Code, generated voice included.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.813
Cutting simple shapes on a laser is easy.

00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:22.917
Turning a picture into cut files takes hours of tracing and guessing.

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:26.320
So Katachi brings Meta’s models to that craft.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.099
Snap a photo.

00:00:29.099 --> 00:00:36.268
Katachi finds the items and layers, cleans them up, lays out sheets for your machine, and guides assembly.

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:41.341
You can say what you want or tap a button: the same actions, with one undo.

00:00:43.241 --> 00:00:46.596
Example one, a layered cut.

00:00:46.596 --> 00:01:05.855
I tell Katachi how to stack it: a solid white base, black with the whiskers cut through, then red, white flowers and gold, every layer keeping the outline.

00:01:05.855 --> 00:01:09.831
Five sheets, built to that plan.

00:01:09.831 --> 00:01:12.441
Less than five cents.

00:01:14.341 --> 00:01:19.578
Example two, a collage of crafts.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:40.684
From one tray photo it finds the earrings, matches the pairs by shape and cuts each pair to one size, with repeated holes evened out.

00:01:40.684 --> 00:01:43.541
About three cents.

00:01:45.441 --> 00:01:51.243
Under the hood: the browser holds the craft and code does all the geometry.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.801
A Cloudflare worker keeps the key server-side.

00:01:54.801 --> 00:01:57.431
Muse Spark reads and plans; SAM 3.

00:01:57.431 --> 00:01:58.282
1 outlines.

00:01:58.282 --> 00:02:00.603
Models never emit coordinates.

00:02:02.503 --> 00:02:08.217
Every edit is one action with one contract, shared by the chat and the buttons.

00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:10.315
Simple phrases run instantly.

00:02:10.315 --> 00:02:16.463
Complex requests go to Muse Spark, which plans the steps as a single undoable change.

00:02:18.363 --> 00:02:22.289
To be clear: this is a prototype, not a finished product.

00:02:22.289 --> 00:02:30.143
The core works, but traces still follow the photo, hidden fretwork is rebuilt solid, and real size is an estimate.

00:02:32.043 --> 00:02:36.048
Three crafts, less than ten cents of Meta model calls.

00:02:36.048 --> 00:02:39.683
The hard part, seeing what to cut, already works.

00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:45.023
Build your world, one sheet at a time, at katachi dot sensei-hq dot com.
